WireTuner: keep each path's even/odd fill flag (the FreeHand importer, D-083).
- FHPath's copy assignment copied the segments, closed flag, transform and style but not
  m_evenOdd (the copy constructor does copy it).  FHCollector::collectPath stores every path by
  assignment (m_paths[recordId] = path), so every collected path came out non-zero even when
  readPath read FreeHand's even/odd bit (the path flag's bit 1), and composite paths, which take
  their first path's rule, lost it with them.

diff -ruN a/libfreehand/src/lib/FHPath.cpp b/libfreehand/src/lib/FHPath.cpp
--- a/libfreehand/src/lib/FHPath.cpp	2026-10-04 11:23:30
+++ b/libfreehand/src/lib/FHPath.cpp	2026-10-04 11:23:30
@@ -662,6 +662,8 @@
   m_isClosed = path.m_isClosed;
   m_xFormId = path.m_xFormId;
   m_graphicStyleId = path.m_graphicStyleId;
+  // WireTuner: the fill rule is copied too (FHCollector::collectPath assigns every path).
+  m_evenOdd = path.m_evenOdd;
   return *this;
 }
 
